WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:12.420
Today we are going to look at 4 amazing examples&nbsp;
of how we are finding new ways to harness the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:20.520
incredible capabilities of OpenAI’s GPT-4 AI&nbsp;
and its ChatGPT assistant. These are things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:27.120
that were not possible at all just a couple&nbsp;
years before today, and are now a reality.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:33.240
One, a dog got diagnosed with a tick-borne&nbsp;
disease, got treatment from a vet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:39.660
but unfortunately, new symptoms developed.&nbsp;
Upon explaining the situation and adding more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:46.200
information about the blood test results for&nbsp;
this good boy, GPT-4 interpreted the results,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:53.580
and made two potential diagnoses for the&nbsp;
dog. A vet was asked to perform the tests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:59.880
and hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;
because the first diagnosis was correct.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:09.420
This good boy has made an almost full recovery&nbsp;
since. Wow. GPT-4 and the vet may have saved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:15.600
this dog’s life. What a time to be alive!&nbsp;
Beyond this being an incredible success story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:25.005
two things really jump out here: one, GPT-3.5,&nbsp;
the previous version was unable to do this, so the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.005 --> 00:01:31.560
recent improvement to this AI are responsible for&nbsp;
this amazing capability. With that, just imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:39.780
what GPT-6 or 7 will be capable of. If you have&nbsp;
any ideas, let me know in the comments below. Two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:46.320
of course, it should not be thought of as a great&nbsp;
doctor, but perhaps a great advisor instead.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:52.980
Two, everybody knows we have text to image,&nbsp;
and some of you Fellow Scholars know even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:02:01.560
text to video. But get this, here is text&nbsp;
to app design. Yes we just write that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:07.320
wish to get an idea for the on-boarding&nbsp;
screen for a dog walking app, and bam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:14.220
we get something quite good immediately. And if&nbsp;
we wish to change it, these designs are editable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:21.480
and what’s more, just imagine how this can be&nbsp;
combined together with the amazing Midjourney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:28.380
or other text to image AIs to populate your&nbsp;
app with beautiful new icons and artworks.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:35.640
Three, GPT-4 is a fantastic writer, and&nbsp;
it can demonstrate its skills when we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:41.700
ask it something that I would not expect&nbsp;
a machine to be able to do. Little AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:48.480
write the most beautiful sentence. It has to&nbsp;
be rhythmically and phonetically beautiful.&nbsp;

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:54.660
“Ephemeral whispers of twilight&nbsp;
danced gracefully upon glistening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:01.620
waves, serenading the eternal stars.”
My goodness. I think most of us would agree that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:08.940
this sentence is indeed beautiful. But I wonder if&nbsp;
this one was a fluke, so I also tried it myself.&nbsp;

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:15.360
“As the sun set over the horizon, the&nbsp;
sky blazed with hues of crimson and gold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:22.740
painting a masterpiece of fleeting beauty.”
This is incredible. And the other two are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:30.720
also amazing. Now, let’s make it a little harder.&nbsp;
Make sure to use the words refraction and caustic.&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:37.140
Interestingly, here it chose to play with the&nbsp;
fact that a caustic can mean bright patterns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:44.760
in nature where an object concentrates light in a&nbsp;
beautiful manner. But, it can also mean sarcastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:52.080
and bitter. So how do you create a beautiful&nbsp;
sentence out of that? It wrote the following:&nbsp;

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.640
“The caustic words of the bitter&nbsp;
old man were like shards of glass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.280
but through the refraction of his&nbsp;
pain, a glimmer of hope still shone.”&nbsp;

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:08.940
Wow, this is a bittersweet sentence that I think&nbsp;
takes a considerable understanding of language,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:14.580
and even the human condition to&nbsp;
write. Wow, this little AI can write.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.680
Four, the improvement from the previous GPT-3.5 is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:25.440
huge when it comes to writing computer&nbsp;
code. It used to write invalid code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:33.720
but the new version, what? Can that really be?&nbsp;
In this particular test, out of a 1000 examples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:42.540
GPT-4 had written zero invalid programs. And what&nbsp;
is also pretty amazing is that about 20% of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:48.000
apps from the previous version were written&nbsp;
in an insecure manner, but for the new one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:56.700
it is down to only 4%. Wow. Now note that this&nbsp;
is not a peer-reviewed experiment and thus, same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:01.260
caveats apply, I put a link to it in the video&nbsp;
description if you would like to have a look.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:08.400
But wait, if it can write secure computer&nbsp;
code, can it also check previously existing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:14.880
projects for flaws? You bet your papers it can!&nbsp;
Look! It can have a look at this piece of code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.620
and tell us block by block what&nbsp;
the potential harms are. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.120
it makes a final assessment as to&nbsp;
what it exactly does as a whole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:31.740
and why it has big problems. Now this is a case&nbsp;
where we can use this AI as a shield. Loving it!

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:38.640
And I have been thinking about that and found that&nbsp;
this is an incredible value proposition. Imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:45.900
if when reading or hearing anything from news&nbsp;
to reports, we could also use it as a shield to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:53.520
fact check everything we hear or read, search for&nbsp;
sources, evaluate the sources, and mark falsehoods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:06:00.060
with red in any article or comment. And the&nbsp;
incredible thing is that I would not be surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:07.980
if that is already possible. GPT-4 has incredible&nbsp;
capabilities and it is all up to our ingenuity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:15.720
to bring out the best from it and help humans,&nbsp;
and yes, doggies too. What a time to be alive!

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:34.740
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

